{
  "id": "Compound::DB00155 - Gene::23564",
  "verbalization": "L-citrulline is implicated in the interaction with multiple Padi proteins, which are involved in the hydrolysis of linear amidines, a specific enzymatic activity. This pathway suggests that L-citrulline may influence the function of Padi1, Padi3, and Padi6, all of which are linked to Ddah2 through their participation in the same enzymatic process. The shared involvement of these Padi proteins in the hydrolysis of amidines implies a potential mechanism by which L-citrulline could modulate Ddah2 activity. The high scores in the paths indicate a strong, consistent relationship, suggesting that L-citrulline may act as a substrate or regulator of the enzymatic activity associated with Ddah2. The evidence supports a direct or indirect relationship between L-citrulline and Ddah2 through its interaction with Padi proteins, which are central to the hydrolysis of amidines.",
